course: dictionary
lesson: 15142
title: Scatterbrain
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A scatterbrain is a person who is forgetful and cannot keep their mind on one thing. «Sam is such a scatterbrain: he left his bag on the bus again.» The clues are left his bag and again. Sam keeps forgetting things, so scatterbrain means someone who forgets and gets distracted.
explain: Look at the two parts of the word. Scatter means to throw things in many directions, and brain is your mind. A scatterbrain's mind jumps about, like thoughts flying everywhere. Check it: put «forgetful person» into the sentence about Sam, and it still makes sense.
explain: This word is informal, so you hear it in chatty talk more than in formal writing. People often say it fondly, as in «You scatterbrain!», but calling someone a scatterbrain again and again can hurt their feelings.
fact: Scatterbrain is a noun: one scatterbrain, two scatterbrains.
fact: Scatterbrain is informal and means a person who is forgetful and disorganised.
fact: «Maya forgot her lunch, her coat and her library book all in one morning.» Maya is scatterbrained, which is the adjective form.
fact: A useful phrase is «a bit of a scatterbrain», which means someone is a little forgetful.
fact: Said kindly, scatterbrain is teasing; said too often, it can hurt.
exercise: «Sam is such a scatterbrain: he left his bag on the bus again.» What is a scatterbrain? | *A person who is forgetful and cannot keep their mind on one thing | A person who is very tall and strong | A person who loves swimming in the sea | A person who always wins at games
exercise: Mum says, «Don't be a scatterbrain, your shoes are by the door!» What is Mum telling you? | You have cleaned your room well | You should go outside to play now | You are very clever at maths | *You have forgotten something and are not thinking clearly
exercise: Which word is the adjective made from scatterbrain? | scattered | brainy | *scatterbrained | scatterbrains
test: Why can calling someone a scatterbrain again and again be unkind? | *It can hurt their feelings | It is a word for animals | It means they are very clever | It is a formal word, so it is rude
test: «Maya forgot her lunch, her coat and her library book all in one morning.» Which word describes Maya? | curt | *scatterbrained | ancient | glum
exam: What does scatterbrain mean? | *A person who is forgetful and cannot keep their mind on one thing | A person who is very old and wise | A tall building with many windows | A person who speaks very quietly and slowly
